  "topIssues": [
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABUPdDJw",
      "title": "interop: update ETHLockbox, SuperchainConfig and OptimismPortal specs for lockbox-based pausing",
      "author": "0xiamflux",
      "number": 950,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "body": "Since ethereum-optimism/optimism#22760, pause state resolves through the `ETHLockbox`. Three specs still describe the old behavior:\n\n- **`interop/eth-lockbox.md`**: `initialize` now takes `(ISuperchainConfig, IOptimismPortal[])`, and the lockbox no longer stores a SystemConfig. `paused()` returns `superchainConfig.isLocalOrGlobalPaused(address(this))`, and `superchainConfig` is stored rather than read through the SystemConfig.\n- **`protocol/superchain-config.md`**: add `isLocalOrGlobalPaused(address)`, which is true if the global pause or the identifier's pause is active.\n- **`interop/optimism-portal.md`**: say that the set shares the first chain's `DelayedWETH`, and that the shared lockbox address is the set's only pause identifier. `OptimismPortal2.paused()` and `superchainConfig()` are both served by the lockbox.\n\nRelated: #937, #943\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-30T21:35:53Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    }
  ],
